  "answer": "Project Zenith is a data analytics initiative aimed at revolutionizing the company's approach to the field. It was introduced by Alex with Sarah Tan as the lead, starting with a kick-off on June 15th and an initial budget of $500,000. The project has since secured a strategic partnership with TechInnovate for AI research. Emily called for innovative ideas, particularly from R&D, to leverage AI in data visualization tools by July 20th. The project reached a significant milestone with the successful completion of the testing phase for a secure file sharing prototype, celebrated on October 10th. The executive board approved a $2 million budget to cover research, development, and marketing. Feedback on the prototype's performance and user experience is being sought by the end of November. Finally, security protocols, including multi-factor authentication and encryption at rest, are being updated to take effect in January."
